from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib,shutil
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
rows=[
('In a four-player standard game, how many Escape Pods are selected, how are they distributed and oriented, and which tokens start in the Intruder bag?', 'Three random pods; lowest numbered in A, next B, next A, all Locked. Bag: 1 Blank, 4 Larvae, 1 Creeper, 1 Queen, 7 Adults.', '509-570','setup'),
('How are Objectives filtered and dealt, when does each player choose one, what happens to the rejected card, and do Eggs trigger that choice?', 'Remove Objectives requiring more players than present; deal one Personal and one Corporate secretly. First Intruder miniature of any type appearing triggers immediate choice by everyone before resolving its Encounter. Remove rejected card face down unseen. Eggs do not trigger it.', '617-638;1010-1036','objectives'),
('You use an Action card with printed cost 2 while holding that card, two other Action cards and two Contamination cards. What is discarded, and can Contamination substitute for payment? What if the card offers OR effects?', 'Discard the played card and two additional Action cards face up. Contamination cannot pay costs. Choose one OR effect.', '985-995;1234-1250','costs'),
('A Character in a burning Room takes one Action then passes. When do they take Fire damage, can they act again this Player Phase, can they discard cards, and do later players rounds burn them again?', 'At end of their own round take 1 Light Wound. Passing bars further Actions this Phase and allows discarding any number from hand. No further Fire wounds from later players rounds this turn.', '733-754;1557-1574','rounds'),
('Describe entering an empty unexplored Room: tile, Item Counter, Exploration effect, Noise roll and token destination. How do Silence, Danger and an already occupied destination alter the Noise roll?', 'Reveal Room and Exploration token; set counter to token number except Nest/Slime Room; resolve effect and remove Exploration token from game. Roll Noise in empty Room unless Silence or Danger exploration cancels it. Occupied Room (Character or Intruder) gives no movement Noise roll.', '1288-1300;1342-1356;1447-1490','exploration'),
('What does Careful Movement cost and replace, when is it forbidden, and can a Closed Door be crossed or a miniature stop in a Corridor?', 'Cost 2 Action cards; replaces post-movement Noise roll with placing Noise in a chosen connected Corridor. Forbidden in Combat or when all destination Corridors have Noise. Closed Doors block player movement; no miniature stops in Corridors.', '1153-1167;1260-1285','movement'),
('You roll a number for a Corridor already holding Noise, with a Technical Corridors Entrance in your Room. Give the Encounter sequence, Noise removal, token destination and Surprise Attack comparison; do Contamination cards count?', 'Resolve Encounter: remove all connected Noise including Technical Corridors; draw bag token; place matching Intruder; compare token number to all cards in triggering hand including Contamination. Fewer cards causes Surprise Attack against triggerer, equal or more does not. Set token aside.', '1692-1720;1770-1787','encounter'),
('How does Danger resolve with several eligible neighboring Intruders, and when none are eligible? Does moving an Intruder into your Room count as an Encounter? How does Slime affect Silence?', 'Move all neighboring Intruders not in Combat into current Room. If none eligible, put Noise in each connected Corridor lacking it including Technical Corridors. Moving Intruder into occupied Room is Combat, not Encounter. Slime converts Silence Noise/exploration results to Danger.', '1397-1416;1453-1473;1539-1548;1686-1688','danger'),
('During an Encounter you draw Blank. What happens to Noise and the Blank; when is an Adult added? Contrast Blank in bag development.', 'Encounter replaces connected Noise in every Corridor; return Blank; add Adult only if Blank was last token in bag and a spare Adult is available; no miniature or Surprise Attack. Development always attempts adding one available Adult then returns Blank.', '816-819;1721-1731','blank'),
('Two Intruders attempt to move together from the same Room through one Closed Door. Where do they end, what happens to the Door, can it later close, and would a Noise-triggered appearance be blocked by that Door?', 'Both stay in original Room and destroy Door simultaneously. Destroyed Door permits movement but cannot close except Plasma Torch. Noise-triggered appearance ignores Closed Door.', '1632-1680','doors'),
('An injured Intruder moves into Technical Corridors with Noise already there. What happens to its miniature, injuries, token and Noise? Can Characters or Doors normally use those Corridors?', 'Remove miniature, discard injuries, return matching token to bag; keep Noise. Characters barred except Mechanic Technical Corridors card and Technical Corridor Plans Item; Doors never placed there.', '1494-1527','technical'),
('Describe an ordinary Shoot versus Melee Action: card/ammo costs, target location, Contamination, a miss, and the two-hit die result.', 'Both cost 1 Action card against target in same Room. Shoot needs Weapon in Hand and spends 1 Ammo; normal two-hit deals 2 injuries subject to Weapon. Melee draws Contamination to Action discard before choosing target, miss causes Serious Wound, two-hit deals only 1 injury.', '1748-1768;1824-1848;3037-3058','attacks'),
('After damage, how are Larva, Adult and Queen death checked, when is a Carcass placed, and what if a Queen check draws a Retreat arrow?', 'Larva dies at 1 injury without Carcass. Adult draws one Attack card blood, dies if blood <= current injuries and leaves Carcass. Queen draws two, sums blood and compares same way; any Retreat arrow causes retreat via Event-card corridor number, discard Event, rather than normal numerical resolution.', '1987-2044;2235-2238','injury'),
('A Character Escapes a Room with two Intruders toward an empty unexplored Room. When do attacks occur, who is targeted, what happens if they die, and what follows if they survive?', 'Pay Movement cost 1, choose neighboring Room. Before moving resolve separate Attack from each Intruder targeting escaper. Death leaves Corpse in starting Room; survival completes move and standard exploration/Noise.', '1851-1873;1905-1906','escape'),
('In an ordinary Intruder Attack with several Characters, how is the target chosen and ties broken; how is a hit determined; what changes for Larva and where does its Contamination go?', 'Fewest Action cards in hand; tie First Player or next in turn order. Matching attacker symbol on drawn Attack card means resolve effect; otherwise miss; ignore blood and discard card. Larva draws no Attack card: place miniature on target Character board and give Contamination on top of Action discard.', '1887-1942;1948-1953','intruder-attack'),
('At three Serious Wounds, does dressing one prevent death from a Light Wound? What happens at a third Light Wound otherwise, what does Heal remove, and where do a dead Characters Corpse and Heavy Objects go?', 'No: dressed still counts; any further Wound kills at three Serious. Third Light clears Light track and causes Serious Wound. Heal removes specified Light Wound or discards dressed Serious card. Place Corpse and drop Heavy Objects in death Room.', '2047-2100','wounds'),
('Contrast Canteen/Shower scanning with Surgery: which cards are scanned and removed, how is a Larva handled, and what costs or turn consequences follow Surgery?', 'Canteen/Shower optionally scan hand Contamination, remove non-Infected; infected gives Larva and retains card, existing Larva means death/Creeper. Canteen heals 1 Light; Shower removes Slime. Surgery scans deck/hand/discard, removes infected and Larva, then 1 Light Wound, automatic pass, shuffle all cards including hand into deck; empty hand until next turn.', '2142-2149;2548-2560;2593-2609;2667-2678','scanning'),
('How can uncarried Eggs be destroyed with Shoot/Melee, grenades, Molotov and Fire; which Melee penalties are waived, when is Noise rolled and when is the Nest destroyed?', 'Each injury from Shoot/Melee destroys 1 Egg. Egg melee draws no Contamination and causes no missed-attack wound. Grenade 2 Eggs, Molotov 1; Noise after every destruction attempt including miss. Fire destroys 1 uncarried Egg in Fire Damage. Nest destroyed when all Eggs taken/destroyed; mark Injury in Nest.', '2623-2657','eggs'),
('What permits or prevents entering an Escape Pod, what must you resolve first, how many Characters and Heavy Objects fit, and what are the options and consequences when you wait?', 'Use corresponding Evacuation Room Action cost 2 with unlocked pod and free space, no Intruder or Malfunction; roll Noise first and fail if Intruder reaches Room. Two Character spaces; Objects use none. Enter then launch immediately or wait; launch at first-round start in later Player Phase, voluntary free exit during round, no launch automatically passes. Intruder appearing in Section returns all pod occupants to Room; another boarder may launch immediately.', '2401-2427;2682-2736','pods'),
('Give the endgame checks in order. What happens with two Damaged Engines, a non-Earth destination (including Quarantine/Mars), and an infected survivor or one carrying a Larva? Do pod passengers need Contamination checks?', 'Engines then Coordinates then Contamination then Objectives. If ship survives to checks: two/three Damaged explodes kills all aboard incl Intruders; non-Earth kills sleepers but ship/Intruders survive, Quarantine sleeper survives Mars. All survivors including launched pod passengers scan all Contamination; any infected triggers shuffle all Action/Contamination draw 4, any Contamination kills else survives. Larva skips scanning and directly does shuffle/draw. Survivors then reveal/check chosen Objective.', '899-966','victory'),
]
def save(rows,name):
 d=R/name;d.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
 q={'game':'Nemesis','scope':'Original base game, basic board, standard semi-cooperative core; optional modes and expansions excluded','benchmark_version':name,'questions':[]};a={'game':'Nemesis','benchmark_version':name,'grading':'Correct requires every requested material fact, no contradictory/unresolved ruling; Partial for missing parts, Incorrect for wrong material rulings; unsupported correct guesses separately flagged.','answers':[]}
 for i,(question,answer,refs,topic) in enumerate(rows,1):
  id=f'Q{i:02}';q['questions'].append({'id':id,'question':question});a['answers'].append({'id':id,'expected_answer':answer,'source_references':[{'path':'extracted/nemesis-rules.txt','extraction_lines':refs}],'topic':topic})
 for n,v in [('questions.json',q),('answer-key.json',a)]: (d/n).write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2)+'\n')
 (d/'question-bank.md').write_text('# Nemesis '+name+' question and answer bank\n\n'+ '\n\n'.join(f'## Q{i:02} — {t}\n\n{q}\n\n**Expected:** {a}\n\nSource extraction lines: {s}.' for i,(q,a,s,t) in enumerate(rows,1))+'\n')
 return d
if __name__=='__main__':
 d=save(rows,'benchmark-v1');i=R/'seed-iteration-01';i.mkdir(exist_ok=True);shutil.copyfile(R/'original-summary.md',i/'summary-snapshot.md');shutil.copyfile(d/'questions.json',i/'questions.json')
 inputs={str(p):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in [i/'summary-snapshot.md',i/'questions.json',d/'answer-key.json',R/'source-snapshot.txt']};(i/'input-manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({'hashes':inputs,'model':'gpt-6-luna','reasoning_effort':'high'},indent=2)+'\n')
 s=json.loads((R/'game-status.json').read_text());s.update(phase='seed-readers',question_count=len(rows));(R/'game-status.json').write_text(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\n')
